WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.200
A good ending can make or break a horror&nbsp;
movie. Fortunately for fright fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.320
the 21st century has been full of fantastic&nbsp;
finales that have sent us scrambling under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:15.920
the covers in fear—and from ghostly apparitions&nbsp;
to bloodthirsty vampires, here are the greatest.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.320
And here's your warning: spoilers&nbsp;
for all these movies, of course.

00:00:21.748 --> 00:00:26.080
The Descent has everything you'd want in a&nbsp;
horror film: plenty of gore, great performances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.160
practical effects... and&nbsp;
two endings? That's right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:35.680
There are two versions of this British horror&nbsp;
film, one released in the U.K. and one in the U.S.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.840
The film comes to a close after our last&nbsp;
surviving character, Sarah spots a shaft of light&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:47.120
atop a hill of bones. Covered in blood,&nbsp;
Sarah makes a mad scramble for the exit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.320
leaving the cave-dwelling creatures behind.&nbsp;
Emerging into the sunlight, Sarah hops in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:57.120
car and makes her great escape, but that all&nbsp;
comes to a screaming halt when she sees the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.400
ghost of her old friend Juno, a woman Sarah just&nbsp;
killed for having an affair with her husband.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.120
That's where the U.S. version ends.&nbsp;
But in the original U.K. version,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.320
there are a few extra scenes that reveal&nbsp;
Sarah never actually escaped the caverns.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:17.680
That whole sequence was just a dream Sarah had&nbsp;
after tumbling down a shaft and hitting her head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.920
In her last moments, Sarah&nbsp;
sees her long-dead daughter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.320
sitting a few feet away, greeting her&nbsp;
mother with a birthday cake. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:31.280
there's no little girl, and the flames from&nbsp;
the birthday candles are really Sarah's torch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:36.400
Sarah is still trapped, and there's no escaping&nbsp;
the crawlers as they move in for the kill. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.800
at least she'll get to share her last few seconds&nbsp;
with her daughter, even if it's all in her head.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:55.120
At first, it might seem like Let the Right&nbsp;
One In ends on an upbeat, romantic note.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:01.840
Two star-crossed lovers — Oskar, a 12-year-old&nbsp;
boy, and Eli, a vampire who looks like a young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:08.160
girl — have just escaped a Swedish town filled&nbsp;
with sadists and snow, bound together by murder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:14.800
and romance. Light-sensitive Eli is hidden away&nbsp;
inside a box, but Oskar keeps the creature company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.320
by tapping out sweet Morse code messages,&nbsp;
letting Eli know they'll always be together.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:25.360
Think about it, though. We've already seen what&nbsp;
happens to people who pledge their lives to Eli.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.000
In the first half of the film, Eli was&nbsp;
palling around with an adult named Hakan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.920
who hunted down humans and drained&nbsp;
them of their blood to keep Eli fed.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:39.680
But Hakan eventually botches a job so badly that&nbsp;
he knows his arrest is imminent; he disfigures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.640
his own face so the cops can't identify him&nbsp;
and won't trace him back to the vampire.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.280
Eventually, the vampire shows up&nbsp;
for a late-night hospital visit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:54.080
and Hakan lets the undead beast feast on&nbsp;
his blood. That's probably what's in store&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:59.120
for Oskar. Sooner or later, Oskar will&nbsp;
dedicate his life to draining people dry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.720
and sooner or later, he'll find&nbsp;
himself haunted by his deeds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:08.960
and replaced by somebody younger after ending up&nbsp;
the next meal for an undead adolescent. Bleak.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:15.600
In Drag Me to Hell, a bank worker named Christine&nbsp;
is cursed after denying a loan extension.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.920
In three days, a demon called the&nbsp;
Lamia will pull Christine into Hell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.440
and he's going to torture her every&nbsp;
second until that devilish date.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:28.320
However, Christine discovers a way to escape&nbsp;
the Lamia's clutches. If she gives the cursed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.520
button away, she can avoid winding up in the&nbsp;
underworld. Ready to get some revenge of her own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:39.280
Christine digs up the now-dead woman's grave who&nbsp;
cursed her and shoves the button down her throat.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:44.240
Only there's one little problem. Christine&nbsp;
has been keeping the button in an envelope.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.600
Unfortunately, her boyfriend has an&nbsp;
identical envelope with a rare coin inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:55.280
and Christine gets the two confused. So after her&nbsp;
late-night cemetery excursion, she goes to meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:59.840
her beau at a train station, and that's when he&nbsp;
casually mentions finding the button in his car.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:06.000
Terrified of what's about to happen, Christine&nbsp;
absolutely freaks out, staggering backwards in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:10.640
shock, tumbling off the railway platform,&nbsp;
and landing on the train tracks below.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:15.520
But before she can get mercifully squished by&nbsp;
an oncoming locomotive, the ground opens up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:20.320
and she's dragged into hell by a mob of&nbsp;
fiery arms. That's how you end a movie.

00:04:22.188 --> 00:04:26.080
Resolution is a deeply unsettling&nbsp;
and underseen film about two friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:31.440
who are trapped in a real-life horror movie. When&nbsp;
graphic designer Michael receives a mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:36.960
video from his junkie friend Chris, Michael&nbsp;
decides it's intervention time. Michael drives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:42.880
out to Chris's country cabin, handcuffs him to&nbsp;
a pipe, and forces his buddy to go cold turkey.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:48.160
However, the intervention veers into spooky&nbsp;
territory when Michael starts discovering photos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.960
records, and slides all around the cabin.&nbsp;
They all depict incredibly creepy stories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:58.080
that usually end in death, and things get&nbsp;
way scarier when Michael and Chris start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.040
finding videos of themselves — videos that&nbsp;
show them getting killed by drug addicts.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.520
The two eventually realize they're&nbsp;
the victims of an evil entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:12.960
that sees them as characters in a horror story.&nbsp;
The duo try their best to outsmart the beast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:16.960
and they certainly seem to. The druggies&nbsp;
who've been threatening them throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:22.240
film are killed, the haunted cabin is set&nbsp;
ablaze, and Chris decides to go to rehab.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:25.280
It's the perfect happy ending,&nbsp;
one they hope will set them free.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:30.720
As the cabin burns to the ground, the entity&nbsp;
rears its monstrous head and confronts the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:34.320
two characters. Desperate for&nbsp;
another chance, Michael begs,

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.840
"Can we try it another way?"

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.800
And that's the end. Creepy.

00:05:44.665 --> 00:05:50.080
The Babadook belongs to a very unique subgenre&nbsp;
of scary films: movies about parents who can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:56.560
stand their kids. The Babadook actually ends on&nbsp;
an upbeat note, unlike many others in this genre.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:01.440
The terrorized mom overcomes her demons and&nbsp;
starts a new life for herself and her son.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.800
Amelia was widowed the same&nbsp;
day she gave birth to her son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:09.840
Samuel. Now, whenever she sees her kid,&nbsp;
she can only think about her dead husband.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:16.160
Needless to say, Amelia isn't handling her grief&nbsp;
well. She's let it fester and grow for so long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:20.960
that there's now a fanged creature with a fondness&nbsp;
for pop-up books hanging around her house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:27.200
The Babadook even possesses Amelia, forcing her to&nbsp;
try and murder Samuel. But after driving the demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:32.800
out, Amelia comes to terms with her grief and&nbsp;
sends the Babadook scurrying down to the basement.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:37.040
In the film's final minutes, we see&nbsp;
a transformed Amelia in her garden.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:42.080
Her anger towards Samuel has disappeared.&nbsp;
Together, the two search their yard for worms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:46.720
and after filling a bowl with the creatures,&nbsp;
Amelia takes the dish down to the basement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:51.040
where she offers the worms to the Babadook.&nbsp;
Even though she's exorcised the beast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:55.440
he's still lurking down there, and just&nbsp;
like Amelia's grief, he'll never go away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.440 --> 00:07:00.144
completely. It's a chilling metaphor for&nbsp;
grief and anger, and a great closing note.

00:07:01.065 --> 00:07:04.080
Horror movies often have twisted endings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.080
but the ending to The Blackcoat's&nbsp;
Daughter is just downright sad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:14.000
This atmospheric film follows two teenage girls&nbsp;
left behind at a boarding school. The semester&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:19.760
is over, but these two are stuck, their parents&nbsp;
nowhere in sight. That's perfectly fine with Rose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:25.520
a senior with a secret she needs to deal with.&nbsp;
But poor Kat isn't handling the abandonment well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:30.640
Thanks to a creepy dream about her parents'&nbsp;
fate, she fears she'll be left alone forever.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:36.240
So naturally, Kat makes a deal with the devil.&nbsp;
The demon makes her commit horrible deeds, but Kat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:42.160
legitimately feels at peace. After she's caught by&nbsp;
the cops, an exorcist kicks the demon out of Kat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:48.400
and even though she begs the spirit to stay, Old&nbsp;
Scratch drifts away, leaving Kat all alone again.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:54.000
Years later, Kat has escaped from a mental&nbsp;
hospital and plans on returning to her school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:59.360
hoping to find her demonic buddy. Along the way,&nbsp;
she's picked up a middle-aged couple, who happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:05.200
to be the parents of Rose, the senior that Kat&nbsp;
decapitated back in the day. Things don't end well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:10.240
for the distraught parents, but when Kat shows&nbsp;
up at the school with two fresh heads in tow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:15.280
the demon is nowhere to be found. That's when&nbsp;
it hits Kat that she'll be alone forever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:19.120
and the film ends with her crying&nbsp;
in the snow, abandoned by everyone.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:25.920
Crimson Peak tells the devastating story of Edith&nbsp;
Cushing, an American heiress who marries charming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:31.840
English aristocrat Thomas Sharpe. Sharpe is an&nbsp;
inventor who lives in a mansion ravaged by time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:36.000
a dying house sinking into the blood&nbsp;
red earth. And when Edith arrives at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:40.800
Sharpe's crumbling estate, she learns she&nbsp;
won't exactly be the lady of the house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:44.560
as Thomas lives with his cold,&nbsp;
calculating sister, Lucille.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:50.080
Actually, Thomas and Lucille are doing way more&nbsp;
than just living together. In addition to having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:55.520
a physical relationship, the penniless siblings&nbsp;
have been keeping afloat by getting Thomas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.520 --> 00:09:00.960
hitched to wealthy women and then killing off the&nbsp;
unlucky brides. Edith discovers she's next on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:06.960
Sharpes' list, but a lovestruck Thomas agrees to&nbsp;
help Edith escape. Lucille offs her brother and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:12.960
confronts Edith, morphing into a ghostly slasher&nbsp;
and fluttering through the fog as Edith holds her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:19.280
off with a knife. Her ghostly brother distracts&nbsp;
her just long enough for Edith to finish her off.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:24.560
Edith then leaves Crimson Peak forever, but&nbsp;
as our hero narrates over the final scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:28.080
we see the dark spirit of&nbsp;
Lucille, sitting at her piano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:33.280
playing a mournful lullaby for time&nbsp;
eternal. Simple, but extremely effective.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:40.480
The Alien series has never been a feel-good&nbsp;
franchise, but when it comes to downbeat endings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:46.720
Alien: Covenant goes darker than any previous&nbsp;
entry. The film focuses on a ship full of humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:51.520
traveling the stars and hoping to wake up&nbsp;
in a new world full of new possibilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:56.800
These sleeping souls have no idea the crew has&nbsp;
made an ill-fated detour to a nearby planet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:01.200
one that's home to killer aliens and&nbsp;
a psychopathic android named David.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:07.200
We first met David in Prometheus, and his disdain&nbsp;
for humans has only grown since the first film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:11.520
He views people simply as subjects for&nbsp;
his experiments, and he'd like to run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:17.040
a few tests on Covenant officer Daniels. She&nbsp;
escapes David's grasp with the help of Walter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:22.480
an android who's the same model as David, only&nbsp;
way better when it comes to his people skills.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:27.840
After Walter defeats David offscreen, he returns&nbsp;
to the Covenant with Daniels and puts her into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:33.840
cryosleep for their long journey ahead. But&nbsp;
moments before going under, Walter's kindly smile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:40.000
morphs into a sadistic smirk, and Daniels&nbsp;
realizes this isn't her robo-buddy after all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:45.520
It's actually David, but there's nothing she&nbsp;
can do as he puts her under. With Daniels out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:51.360
of the way, David coughs up two alien embryos&nbsp;
and strolls through the massive cryochamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.000
admiring the pods full of sleeping colonists.&nbsp;

00:10:55.280 --> 00:11:02.000
"Don't let the bed bugs bite.&nbsp;
I'll tuck in the children."

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:07.680
M. Night Shyamalan movies are always judged&nbsp;
on the strength of their endings. He's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:11.280
occasionally struggled with sticking&nbsp;
the landing since The Sixth Sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:14.160
but Shyamalan recaptured some&nbsp;
of that glory with Split.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:18.800
This 2017 hit follows a&nbsp;
disturbed dude named Kevin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:24.320
a man with 24 personalities bouncing around his&nbsp;
brain. Some are friendly, some are dangerous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:29.840
but the dreaded Beast is a straight-up monster&nbsp;
— a cannibalistic creature who can scale walls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:35.600
bend metal, and deflect gunshots. In the final&nbsp;
three minutes of the film, after the climactic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:40.880
showdown with Casey Cooke, we watch as Kevin&nbsp;
examines himself in a mirror, awestruck that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:45.920
he's just survived a shotgun blast to the chest.&nbsp;
And that's where the movie proper ends, with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:51.200
Kevin's evil personalities basking in their new&nbsp;
abilities and plotting their war on the impure.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:56.240
"Let him show the world how powerful we can be."

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:59.920
That right there would be a killer&nbsp;
ending, but it's made even better by an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:04.880
extra scene at a diner. The horrified patrons&nbsp;
are watching a news report about the Beast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:11.280
one customer is reminded of Mr. Glass, the mad&nbsp;
genius from Shyamalan's 2002 film Unbreakable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:16.480
And that's when we see David Dunn, sipping coffee&nbsp;
at the end of the bar and realizing it's time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:22.800
to grab his green raincoat. In just one minute,&nbsp;
the entire fabric of the film has been changed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:28.320
Split wasn't just a freaky horror movie - it&nbsp;
was a stealth sequel to Unbreakable all along.

00:12:29.753 --> 00:12:34.080
Mother is one part Biblical allegory,&nbsp;
one part environmental metaphor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:39.440
and totally disturbing from beginning to end.&nbsp;
Jennifer Lawrence stars as the titular Mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:44.160
wife of a beloved poet known simply as Him.&nbsp;
However, their little world is threatened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:49.440
by the arrival of an entire host of odd&nbsp;
people, intent on destroying their home.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:53.760
Once you realize that Mother&nbsp;
represents Mother Earth and Him is God,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:59.120
things start clicking into place. The film&nbsp;
rehashes several well known Biblical tales.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:04.640
When Mother's newborn baby is murdered by the&nbsp;
masses, that's symbolic of Christ's crucifixion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:09.920
All the people Him has welcomed into his home&nbsp;
begin destroying everything in sight — desecrating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:14.320
the planet Earth, if you will. And Mother&nbsp;
can only take so much abuse for so long.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:19.840
After the death of her baby, Mother snaps&nbsp;
and fights back by setting the house on fire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:25.760
The house is burned to ash, the people are purged&nbsp;
away by flames, but since Him is an immortal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:31.680
being, he survives without a single burn. The&nbsp;
all-powerful poet picks up Mother's charred body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:37.280
and removes a crystal from her chest, taking&nbsp;
the last of her love so he can rebuild his home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:42.240
create a new wife, and start over again.&nbsp;
And that's how this horror show ends, with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:47.840
the cycle beginning anew, all because Him craves&nbsp;
praise and affection for his literary creations.

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:51.179
"Baby?"

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:57.120
A Quiet Place was a critical and commercial&nbsp;
smash when it hit theaters in 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:00.640
and one of the reasons the film was&nbsp;
so successful is the fact that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:04.000
features one of the most memorable&nbsp;
endings in horror movie history.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:09.360
A Quiet Place focuses on the Abbott family,&nbsp;
who are trying to survive in a world plagued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:15.360
by monsters. These extraterrestrial creatures are&nbsp;
blind, but their sense of hearing is incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:20.800
acute. Knock over a lantern, trip on the stairs,&nbsp;
or shout in pain, and they'll slice you in half.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:29.840
On top of that, they're covered in natural&nbsp;
armor, making them nearly impossible to kill.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:34.720
As a result, the Abbotts must adapt&nbsp;
to live in a world without sound,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.360
keeping as quiet as possible at all times.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:43.200
Because the creatures' ears are so sensitive, they&nbsp;
can't stand the feedback from Regan's cochlear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:47.840
implants. So when she and the surviving family&nbsp;
members are trapped in a basement by one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:54.080
beasts, Regan uses her hearing aid to drive one of&nbsp;
the monsters crazy. It starts to writhe in pain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:58.240
allowing Regan's mother to kill the&nbsp;
weakened creature with a shotgun blast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:03.280
Of course, the gunshot attracts the other nearby&nbsp;
aliens, but the Abbotts aren't afraid. They've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:08.560
got the upper hand, and as the evil E.T.s make&nbsp;
a beeline for the basement, Regan gets her new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:13.360
weapon ready — and her mom racks another shell&nbsp;
into her shotgun, ready to make some noise.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:20.880
For all its sci-fi trappings, Annihilation is very&nbsp;
much a horror movie. It's got hideous mutants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:25.920
extreme body horror, and uber-creepy plant&nbsp;
people. But perhaps the most terrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:31.120
scene comes when Natalie Portman encounters a&nbsp;
mysterious being that mirrors her every move.

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:33.520
Annihilation finds Portman playing Lena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:38.880
a soldier-turned-scientist who's haunted by&nbsp;
guilt and regret. Her military husband, Kane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:44.640
has disappeared after venturing into the Shimmer.&nbsp;
Lena blames herself for Kane's disappearance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:48.400
as her bad choices might've driven&nbsp;
her husband to a suicide mission.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:54.480
But a year after vanishing, Kane reappears —&nbsp;
confused, missing memories, and incredibly sick.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:16:02.320
"I don't know where it was or what it was."

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:03.360
"How is that possible?"

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:09.120
Wanting to know what happened to Kane, Lena&nbsp;
joins a scientific team heading into the Shimmer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:14.720
which refracts and combines everything from&nbsp;
memories to DNA. She eventually winds up at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:20.480
a lighthouse where she meets a metallic humanoid&nbsp;
that copies her movements and steals her likeness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:25.040
A horrified Lena tries to escape,&nbsp;
but the humanoid won't let her leave.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:29.280
It even pins her against the door,&nbsp;
suffocating Lena with the weight of its body.

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:32.560
She escapes, but this is&nbsp;
where things get ambiguous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:37.280
Did the real Lena escape, or is this&nbsp;
her double? When she hugs her husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:43.760
both their eyes dance and change colors, just like&nbsp;
the Shimmer. So is this the real Lena? Ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:48.960
it really doesn't matter. The only thing that&nbsp;
does is that Lena has changed. The woman who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:54.400
walked into the Shimmer has come out a completely&nbsp;
different person. Confusing but fascinating.

00:16:55.992 --> 00:16:59.840
Upgrade is set in a near future where&nbsp;
most humans are totally cool with having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:05.360
technological implants. One exception&nbsp;
is Grey Trace, but after a gang of thugs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:10.640
kill his wife and leave him paralyzed, Grey&nbsp;
finds himself totally reliant on technology.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:16.400
Thanks to an oddly benevolent billionaire,&nbsp;
Grey has been implanted with an AI named STEM.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:22.880
STEM connects Grey's brain to his body, allowing&nbsp;
him to move around for the first time in months.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:27.280
He's also oddly keen on helping Grey&nbsp;
find his wife's killers. Together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:32.160
the two stalk the streets, dishing out grisly&nbsp;
deaths to the crooks who ruined Grey's life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:37.360
However, at the end of the film, Grey discovers&nbsp;
STEM has been pulling the strings all along.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:41.840
The AI desperately wanted to be human&nbsp;
and thought Grey was the perfect host,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:46.800
so he turned the mechanic into a widowed&nbsp;
quadriplegic. And once he got inside Grey's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:51.920
brain, he murdered anyone who knew of his&nbsp;
existence, from the killers to his creator.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:56.960
Holding tight to his last shreds of humanity,&nbsp;
Grey fights back, desperately trying to save&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:03.280
an innocent detective. In that struggle, Grey's&nbsp;
mind finally breaks. His brain goes limp, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:09.280
STEM locks him away in a dream world, a paradise&nbsp;
where his wife is still alive. In some ways, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:14.960
a happy ending for Grey, but also horrifying when&nbsp;
you realize that STEM has achieved his final goal.

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:20.320
"Grey's not here anymore, he's in a better&nbsp;
place, in his mind where he wants to be."

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:26.400
Hereditary is a tough watch of a film with an&nbsp;
incredibly deranged ending. Basically, the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:32.000
follows a doomed family that's being manipulated&nbsp;
into bringing a demon named Paimon into the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:36.960
He's been possessing a little girl named Charlie&nbsp;
for a few years, but Paimon would prefer to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:42.560
possess a male, so his followers plot to transfer&nbsp;
the spirit into Charlie's older brother, Peter.

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:46.880
Of course, that involves a rather complicated&nbsp;
ritual where you have to decapitate Charlie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:51.680
host a disturbing seance, and set a man on&nbsp;
fire. In the last few minutes of Hereditary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:54.240
Peter is chased around the&nbsp;
house by his possessed mom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.800 --> 00:19:00.320
Everywhere he runs, he keeps bumping into naked,&nbsp;
aging cult members. And to cap everything off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:04.720
Peter watches in horror as his mom&nbsp;
saws her own head off with a wire.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:06.400
He's having a rough night.

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:09.760
It's all too much for Peter,&nbsp;
who throws himself out a window&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:15.440
and ends up getting controlled by Paimon anyway.&nbsp;
In the film's final scene, a possessed Peter is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:20.320
surrounded by worshipful cult members, the&nbsp;
beheaded corpses of his mom and grandmother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:26.000
and a freaky shrine that prominently features&nbsp;
Charlie's decapitated head. Wholesome family fun.

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:34.240
"All I do is worry, and slave and defend you, and&nbsp;
all I get back is that f---ing face on your face!"

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:40.320
Mandy is a bloodsoaked acid trip of a&nbsp;
movie that blends a whole host of genres,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:46.560
but in its heavy metal heart, Mandy is a horror&nbsp;
film. The film boasts Nicolas Cage as Red Miller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:51.200
who wants revenge for his murdered wife,&nbsp;
Mandy. Since we're talking about Nic Cage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:56.720
that means doing battle with demons and getting&nbsp;
into chainsaw fights with psycho hippies.

00:19:56.720 --> 00:20:01.840
From the moment his wife is immolated, Red&nbsp;
begins to lose his mind. It doesn't help any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:07.200
when he samples some of the world's trippiest LSD,&nbsp;
which plunges him deep into the cosmic darkness.

00:20:13.840 --> 00:20:18.640
His eyes become fireballs of rage, and in&nbsp;
the film's final minutes, he hunts down the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:24.320
members of the hippie cult that killed his wife&nbsp;
and puts his freshly-forged axe to good use.

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:28.320
When he finally confronts the&nbsp;
insecure cult leader, Jeremiah Sand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:32.960
he crushes the man's skull with his hands&nbsp;
before setting Sand's church on fire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:38.240
As the building burns down, for a moment,&nbsp;
everything is peaceful. The blood is gone from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:43.600
his face, and he sees the spirit of Mandy riding&nbsp;
shotgun. He flashes back to the moment they first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:48.800
met at a club, wearing identical T-shirts,&nbsp;
but then reality comes crashing back hard.

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:55.040
Red is still soaked with gore and grinning like&nbsp;
a madman. And as he drives off to nowhere, we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:55.040 --> 00:21:01.120
see two eerie planets hanging over the horizon. Is&nbsp;
this another world? Is it all in his head? It's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:06.880
truly freaky moment, and one that's bound to stir&nbsp;
up debate among horror fans for years to come.

